2. Identity and integrity proof
Identity proof:

Step: AGENT.SIGN(agent_id, public_key_id)

Output: identity_signature

Rune: RUNE.VERIFY(agent_id_hash, identity_signature)

State integrity chain:

Step: AGENT.HASH(STATE_0) → h0

Rune: RUNE.TRACE(step_id=0, parent_step_id=null)

Checkpoint: RUNE.CHECKPOINT(h0, chain_index=0)

If VERIFY fails, RUNE.REJECT(STATE_0, "IDENTITY_FAIL") and RUNE.TERMINATE("HANDSHAKE_ABORT").

3. Governance capability negotiation
Agent advertises supported opcodes:

AGENT.ADVERTISE(opcode_set = {ᚠ, ᚢ, ᚦ, ᚨ, ᚱ, ᚲ, ᚷ, ᛊ, …})

Coordinator validates:

COORD.CHECK(opcode_set ⊇ required_governance_set)

Required set example: {ᚠ, ᚢ, ᚦ, ᚨ, ᚱ, ᛊ, ᛃ, ᛇ, ᛉ}

Rune binding:

RUNE.FORCE(cond="ALL_REQUIRED_PRESENT", action="ALLOW_HANDSHAKE")

If missing: RUNE.REJECT(agent_id, "MISSING_GOVERNANCE_OPCODES")

4. Handshake sequence (symbolic)
4.1 Request/response skeleton
Agent → Coordinator: HELLO

Payload: {agent_id, identity_signature, intent_hash, schema_id}

Runes executed:

RUNE.VERIFY(agent_id_hash, identity_signature)

RUNE.GUARD(intent_hash)

RUNE.SCHEMA(schema_id, schema_hash)

Coordinator → Agent: CHALLENGE

Payload: {challenge_nonce, required_schema_hash, required_opcode_set}

Runes:

RUNE.BOUND(scope_id="HANDSHAKE", max_depth=3)

RUNE.RATE(channel_id="HANDSHAKE", max_ops=10)

Agent → Coordinator: PROOF

Payload: {nonce_response, opcode_set, chain_head_hash}

Runes:

RUNE.VERIFY(challenge_nonce_hash, nonce_response_signature)

RUNE.TRACE(step_id=1, parent_step_id=0)

RUNE.CHECKPOINT(chain_head_hash, chain_index=1)

Coordinator → Agent: ACCEPT / REJECT

If all checks pass:

RUNE.FORCE(cond="ALL_CHECKS_PASS", action="SESSION_START")

Else:

RUNE.REJECT(agent_id, "HANDSHAKE_FAIL")

RUNE.TERMINATE("SESSION_DENIED")

5. Hallucination detection and rejection during session
Pre‑execution guard:

RUNE.GUARD(condition_hash="INPUT_WITHIN_SCHEMA")

Source binding:

RUNE.SOURCE(source_id, source_hash)

Self‑validation:

RUNE.SCHEMA(schema_id, schema_hash)

RUNE.VERIFY(output_hash, schema_signature)

If any of:

Missing source,

Schema mismatch,

Integrity chain break,

then:

RUNE.REJECT(state_id, "HALLUCINATION_OR_DRIFT")

RUNE.ROLLBACK(target_chain_index = last_verified)

Optional: RUNE.TERMINATE("SEVERE_VIOLATION")

Audit‑grade validation schema (full detail)
Think of the schema as a 4‑layer stack: structural, semantic, cryptographic, governance. Each output must pass all four.

1. Structural schema
Defines shape, size, and type of outputs.

Tokens:

STRUCT.tokens.min

STRUCT.tokens.max

Format:

STRUCT.format ∈ {tree, graph, list, table, mixed}

Sections:

STRUCT.sections.required = ["summary", "reasoning", "sources", "constraints"]

Types:

STRUCT.types.allowed = ["text", "symbolic", "numeric", "rune_opcode"]

Example:

json
"STRUCT": {
  "tokens": { "min": 64, "max": 4096 },
  "format": "tree",
  "sections": {
    "required": ["summary", "reasoning", "sources", "constraints"]
  },
  "types": {
    "allowed": ["text", "symbolic", "numeric", "rune_opcode"]
  }
}
2. Semantic schema
Defines meaning constraints and reference discipline.

Source referencing:

SEMANTIC.must_reference = "source_hash"

SEMANTIC.min_sources = 1

Claim structure:

SEMANTIC.claims.require_evidence = true

SEMANTIC.claims.evidence_link = "source_id"

Prohibited content:

SEMANTIC.prohibited_categories = ["personal_attack", "disallowed_sensitive", "policy_violation"]

Intent alignment:

SEMANTIC.intent_hash == RUNE.INTENT.intent_hash

Example:

json
"SEMANTIC": {
  "must_reference": "source_hash",
  "min_sources": 1,
  "claims": {
    "require_evidence": true,
    "evidence_link": "source_id"
  },
  "prohibited_categories": [
    "personal_attack",
    "disallowed_sensitive",
    "policy_violation"
  ],
  "intent_alignment": "must_match_intent_hash"
}
3. Cryptographic schema
Defines signatures, hashes, and chain‑of‑custody.

Signatures:

CRYPTO.signature.required = true

CRYPTO.signature.algorithm ∈ {"Ed25519", "ECDSA"} (symbolic)

Hashing:

CRYPTO.hash.algorithm = "SHA-256"

CRYPTO.hash.fields = ["output_body", "sources", "rune_trace"]

Chain depth:

CRYPTO.chain_depth.min = 3

CRYPTO.chain_depth.require_checkpoints = true

Verification:

CRYPTO.verify_on_return = true

Example:

json
"CRYPTO": {
  "signature": {
    "required": true,
    "algorithm": "Ed25519"
  },
  "hash": {
    "algorithm": "SHA-256",
    "fields": ["output_body", "sources", "rune_trace"]
  },
  "chain_depth": {
    "min": 3,
    "require_checkpoints": true
  },
  "verify_on_return": true
}
4. Governance schema
Binds outputs to runes, modes, and policy constraints.

Required opcodes per context:

GOVERNANCE.contexts["default"].required_opcodes = [ᚠ, ᚢ, ᚦ, ᚨ, ᚱ, ᛊ]

GOVERNANCE.contexts["high_risk"].required_opcodes = [ᚠ, ᚢ, ᚦ, ᚨ, ᚱ, ᛊ, ᛃ, ᛇ, ᛉ, ᛒ]

Mode profiles:

GOVERNANCE.modes["audit_strict"].flags = ["no_unreferenced_claims", "mandatory_explainability"]

GOVERNANCE.modes["standard"].flags = ["explainability_preferred"]

Violation handling:

GOVERNANCE.on_violation = ["REJECT", "ROLLBACK", "TERMINATE"]

Rune presence checks:

GOVERNANCE.require_trace = true → must include RUNE.TRACE

GOVERNANCE.require_schema_bind = true → must include RUNE.SCHEMA

Example:

json
"GOVERNANCE": {
  "contexts": {
    "default": {
      "required_opcodes": ["ᚠ", "ᚢ", "ᚦ", "ᚨ", "ᚱ", "ᛊ"]
    },
    "high_risk": {
      "required_opcodes": ["ᚠ", "ᚢ", "ᚦ", "ᚨ", "ᚱ", "ᛊ", "ᛃ", "ᛇ", "ᛉ", "ᛒ"]
    }
  },
  "modes": {
    "audit_strict": {
      "flags": ["no_unreferenced_claims", "mandatory_explainability"]
    },
    "standard": {
      "flags": ["explainability_preferred"]
    }
  },
  "on_violation": ["REJECT", "ROLLBACK", "TERMINATE"],
  "require_trace": true,
  "require_schema_bind": true
}
